 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "lg w/d keeps saying dE n wont start?? door is shut"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I cannot confirm what DE means on your specific LG model as it is not in my standard error list, so we will focus on why it won't start with the door shut. The most common cause for a locked door that won't release is simply a safety delay after a cycle or an active child lock. Please leave the machine switched on and wait five minutes to see if the lock releases naturally. If it remains locked, switch it off at the wall socket, wait another five minutes, then try opening the door again."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "its not locked, it just wont start. it clicks then nothing. its got a king size duvet in if that matters"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Since you have confirmed the door is shut but not locked, the DE message may just be a display code or part of the model name rather than an active error. A king-size duvet is very likely to cause this because it absorbs water and sticks to one side, making the machine think the load is unbalanced so it refuses to start. This is normal behaviour designed to protect the drum from shaking too much. Please open the door and redistribute the duvet evenly around the drum before trying again."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok but dE is on the screen, not just the name. i can try moving it round, its bulging against the glass n a corner is squashed in the seal tho"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Before you start, switch it off and unplug it. I cannot confirm what DE means on your specific LG model as it is not in my standard error list, so we will focus on why it won't start with the door shut. The fact that the duvet is bulging and squashed in the seal suggests it may be physically preventing the door from latching properly or triggering a safety sensor. Please open the door, remove the duvet to clear any blockage, and ensure nothing is caught in the rubber seal before closing it firmly until you hear it click."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok ive taken the duvet out n tried towels instead and it starts fine. so is it just the duvet being too big?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, that was exactly the issue as king-size duvets often cause an unbalanced load which stops the machine from starting. I am glad to hear it is working fine now with the towels instead. To stop this happening again, try spreading the washing out evenly or adding a few smaller items to help balance the drum. Is there anything else I can help you with today?"
  }
